From: JiaxinD <djx2048@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 20:51:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] perf: capture-safe GPU radix hash for generated rows (per
 @gaoyang07 review)

The generated-row radix key reused the prompt-path blake2b helper
(build_row_cache_key_ids), which moves the row tensor to host (.numpy())
and hashes per frame. On the decode hot path that is a GPU->CPU sync every
frame, blocking CUDA-graph capture / async-decode (#734/#736).

- new radix_hash.py: fixed-coefficient int64 Horner hash, folds < 151643,
  EOS rows keep the raw audio_end id; pure tensor ops (no .cpu()/.item()/
  numpy), CUDA-graph capturable, no int64 overflow.
- model_runner._row_radix_token_ids delegates to it; the prompt-path
  blake2b (build_row_cache_key_ids) is intentionally unchanged.
- CPU key-layer tests: determinism, collision, EOS, domain, dtype/device.
- docs/design/gpu_radix_hash.md: capture-safety + collision analysis +
  two-layer verification (GPU output-layer rerun is PENDING).
